@using MudBlazor
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web

<h3>Button dimensions: reuse the owning page's style</h3>
<p>No universal fixed width is established. Text buttons grow with their label; do not truncate or force every action to the same width.
    Account actions and compact Product controls intentionally differ. These measurements describe existing implementations, not new global rules.</p>
<div class="catalog-table" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Button sizing reference">
    <table>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Existing use</th><th scope="col">Height / width</th><th scope="col">Padding / icons</th><th scope="col">Source</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row">Account primary action</th><td>min-height: 44px; width automatic; inherited min-width: 64px</td><td>Medium Filled: 6px vertical / 16px horizontal; start/end icon 20px</td><td><code>Features/Identity/Users/CreateUser.razor</code> plus MudBlazor defaults</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Compact Product text button</th><td>height and min-height: 36px; width automatic; inherited min-width: 64px</td><td>4px vertical; horizontal remains 16px Filled / 8px Text (Medium); start/end icon 20px</td><td><code>wwwroot/css/app.css</code>: <code>.product-button.mud-button-root</code></td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Compact Product icon button</th><td>36 × 36px</td><td>6px; <code>Size.Small</code> as used by DescriptionEditor; Material SVG 20px at a 16px root font</td><td><code>wwwroot/css/app.css</code>: <code>.product-button.mud-icon-button</code></td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Product controls on coarse pointers</th><td>44px hit-target height; icon hit target 44 × 44px</td><td>4px transparent border retains the compact painted surface; background-clip: padding-box; no shadow</td><td><code>wwwroot/css/app.css</code>: <code>@@media (pointer: coarse)</code></td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>
<p>Paths above are relative to <code>src/Retravion.Web/</code>. Inherited measurements come from pinned MudBlazor 9.11.0
    <code>MudBlazor.min.css</code>: <code>.mud-button</code>, <code>.mud-button-text</code>,
    <code>.mud-button-icon-size-medium</code>, and <code>.mud-icon-size-small</code>.
    MudBlazor Small/Medium/Large start/end icons are 18/20/22px; standalone SVG Small/Medium/Large icons are 1.25/1.5/2.25rem.
    These are library defaults, not newly established app rules. Recheck them on library upgrades.
    Height is a minimum for account actions, not a text-clipping constraint. Preserve readable labels and touch targets.</p>
<div class="catalog-examples">
    <MudButton Variant="Variant.Filled" Color="Color.Primary" Style="min-height:44px" StartIcon="@Icons.Material.Outlined.Check">Account-size example</MudButton>
    <MudButton Variant="Variant.Filled" Color="Color.Primary" Class="product-button" StartIcon="@Icons.Material.Outlined.Check">Compact Product example</MudButton>
    <MudIconButton Icon="@Icons.Material.Outlined.VerticalSplit" Class="product-button" Size="Size.Small" aria-label="Compact Product icon example" title="Compact Product icon example" />
</div>
<pre><code>@SizeSnippet</code></pre>

<h3>Default, hover, keyboard focus, and pressed</h3>
<p>These are real browser states on the same enabled button below—not manually painted imitations.
    Hover with the pointer, Tab to focus, and hold the pointer down or hold Space while focused to see pressed feedback.
    Enter or release Space activates the button. Use browser responsive/coarse-pointer emulation to inspect the touch target above.</p>
<MudButton id="catalog-state-button" Variant="Variant.Filled" Color="Color.Primary" Style="min-height:44px"
           @onmouseenter="@(() => _state = "Hover: pointer is over the button.")"
           @onmouseleave="@(() => _state = "Default: pointer left the button.")"
           @onfocus="@(() => _state = "Keyboard focus: this button receives the next keyboard action.")"
           @onblur="@(() => _state = "Default: focus left the button.")"
           @onpointerdown="@(() => _state = "Pressed: pointer is held down; this is not a persistent selection.")"
           @onpointerup="@(() => _state = "Hover: pointer released.")"
           @onpointercancel="@(() => _state = "Default: pointer interaction cancelled.")"
           OnClick="@(() => _state = "Activated: example only; no data changed.")">Try button states</MudButton>
<p role="status">@_state</p>
<p>Filled Primary uses the theme primary color by default and its darken token for hover/focus/active feedback.
    MudBlazor supplies hover and pressed elevation/ripple behavior.
    Keyboard focus additionally uses <code>:focus-visible</code> in <code>wwwroot/css/app.css</code>
    (3px outline, 4px offset, with dark-theme handling). Never remove focus indication.</p>

<h3>Disabled, loading, and selected are different</h3>
<div class="catalog-examples">
    <MudButton Variant="Variant.Filled" Color="Color.Primary" Disabled="true" Style="min-height:44px">Disabled example</MudButton>
    <MudButton Variant="Variant.Filled" Color="Color.Primary" Disabled="true" Style="min-height:44px" aria-busy="true">
        <MudProgressCircular Indeterminate="true" Size="Size.Small" Class="mr-2" aria-hidden="true" /> Saving example…
    </MudButton>
</div>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Disabled:</strong> native disabled button; cannot activate or receive Tab focus. Explain the unmet condition in nearby text, not color alone.</li>
    <li><strong>Loading:</strong> operation in progress; disable repeat submission, keep a readable action label, and show status. The create/edit templates below demonstrate a held busy state.</li>
    <li><strong>Selected / highlighted:</strong> persistent choice, not hover, focus, or an operation's momentary pressed state. In the live Markdown example, Side by side / Stacked uses <code>aria-pressed="true"</code>, Primary icons, and the existing selected background. Switch between them to inspect selection.</li>
</ul>
<p>Selected styling source: <code>src/Retravion.Web/Features/Product/Description/DescriptionEditor.razor</code> and its
    <code>.razor.css</code> rule <code>[aria-pressed="true"]</code>. Preserve that contract rather than inventing another highlight style.</p>

@code {
    private string _state = "Default: ready for interaction.";
    private const string SizeSnippet = """
        <!-- Account action: below its card -->
        <MudButton Variant="Variant.Filled" Color="Color.Primary" Style="min-height:44px">Save</MudButton>
        <!-- Product action: reuse the existing app.css class, including coarse-pointer rules -->
        <MudButton Variant="Variant.Filled" Color="Color.Primary" Class="product-button">Save</MudButton>
        <MudIconButton Icon="@Icons.Material.Outlined.VerticalSplit" Class="product-button"
                       Size="Size.Small" aria-label="Side by side" title="Side by side" />
        """;
}
